        "original_id": "03557034-979c-5e8e-81b4-88bdbe7d8a91",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Eleutherococcus, Amaryllis, Chengiopanax sciadophylloides\n- Taxonomy: genus, species, family Araliaceae, subtribe Amaryllidinae, tribe Amaryllideae, ITS sequence data\n\nFacts:\n- Eleutherococcus is a genus of 38 species of thorny shrubs and trees in the family Araliaceae.\n- Amaryllis is the only genus in the subtribe Amaryllidinae of the tribe Amaryllideae.\n- Chengiopanax sciadophylloides was previously included in the genus Eleutherococcus.\n- Chengiopanax sciadophylloides is distinguished from Eleutherococcus by lacking spines or prickles.\n- ITS sequence data confirmed the separation of Chengiopanax sciadophylloides from Eleutherococcus.",
